& [SJS]
  + Situation: historical lineage identity ends at Slice6G while the provider-free shell now includes custody query and measurement layers
  + Justification: an additive release root can summarize the complete current boundary without rewriting predecessor evidence or implying new capability
  + Solution: commit regenerated roots metrics profiles operation names and ordered proof-file identities in one strict digest-only manifest

& [Delineation]
  + release manifest summarizes evidence and does not embed or replace it
  + compile-time proof bytes are repository identity evidence and not external provenance or signatures
  + provider-free release candidate is not live provider runtime release
  + capability denials remain authoritative regardless of release-root presence

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + use exact upstream validators and normalized compact JSON digests
  + proof commitments retain ordinal label path byte count and SHA-256 digest only
  + release root commits ordered deterministic fields under one domain separator
  + strict reconstruction refuses drift in any upstream identity or capability

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty preserves historical root meaning and names the release boundary narrowly
  + Security binds exact upstream roots profiles operations metrics proof bytes and denials
  + Planner orders all dependencies and seventeen proof commitments
  + Weaver composes distinct evidence identities beneath one release root
  + Scribe makes the current shell catalogue inspectable without body duplication
  + Refiner emits only release-relevant commitments and boundaries
  + Observer regenerates every upstream form before admitting the manifest

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated provider-free release manifest generator validator serializer artifact CLI and adversarial tests
  + keep discovery live provider physical storage tokenizer performance and effects outside authority

& [Rollback]
  + additive module artifact CLI branch exports and tests remove without changing predecessor behavior
